  logic worth testing is testable without a browser. [38;5;153mstore.js[39m being a narrow interface is also the seam where a
  server-backed implementation would slot in, if you ever reverse the no-backend call.

  [1mTask shape:[0m

  {
    [36mid[39m: [31m"uuid"[39m,            [32m// crypto.randomUUID()[39m
    [36mtitle[39m: [31m"string"[39m,
    [36mdone[39m: [34mfalse[39m,
    [36mdueAt[39m: [31m"2026-09-25T17:00:00.000Z"[39m,  [32m// ISO 8601, or null[39m
    [36mcreatedAt[39m: [31m"2026-09-22T11:02:00.000Z"[39m
  }

  [38;5;153mdueAt[39m is nullable — a task with no due date simply never notifies. Times are stored as UTC ISO strings and rendered in
  local time; storing local-formatted strings is the classic bug here.

  [1mPersistence:[0m one [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m key, [38;5;153mtasks.v1[39m, holding a JSON array. Loaded once at startup, written on every mutation.
  The version suffix exists so a future shape change can migrate rather than silently misread old data. A corrupt or
  absent value falls back to an empty list rather than throwing — a bad key should not make the app unopenable.

  One open decision inside this section:
